# __BUILD__

__LIBRARY__ building the comparison screen in __FRAMEWORK__.

Read [`spec/screen-spec.md`](../../spec/screen-spec.md) before writing code. Sections 2 to 9 are the requirements. A requirement this library cannot meet is recorded as a failure, not worked around.

```
pnpm --filter @uilc/__BUILD__ dev
pnpm --filter @uilc/__BUILD__ test
pnpm --filter @uilc/__BUILD__ build
pnpm --filter @uilc/__BUILD__ measure
```

Write only inside this folder and `results/__BUILD__.json`. `packages/criteria` and `packages/harness` belong to the phase one owner.

## Notes for the write-up

Keep a running list here as you build: what the library gave for free, what had to be hand built, and where a spec requirement fought the defaults. The write-up is assembled from these once all eight results exist.

## comparison.json

`measure` reads the bundle and the ergonomics counts off the code. Two things it cannot see live in `comparison.json`: how many section 9 requirements needed custom code, and whether the modal, select, and toast came from __LIBRARY__ or were hand built. Update it as you go rather than at the end.
